Existing entity names include "Lena". "Lena Fischer" is presumably the same person as "Lena" — the note uses a different name. So I should add an entity alias: name "Lena Fischer", canonical "Lena".

New durable fact: "Lena is the release captain for Q1 2026." Entities: Lena (and maybe "Q1 2026"? Q1 2026 is a time period, not really an entity — probably skip; but could include as a fact about Lena only).

Relations? "release captain" isn't a relation to another entity; Q1 2026 could be an entity but it's a time. I'd just add the fact.

So patch:
{
 "add_facts": [
   {
     "content": "Lena is the release captain for Q1 2026.",
     "entities": ["Lena"],
     "kind": "fact",
     "confidence": 1,
     "evidence": "Lena Fischer is the release captain for Q1 2026."
   }
 ],
 "entity_aliases": [
   {
     "name": "Lena Fischer",
     "canonical": "Lena",
     "evidence": "Lena Fischer is the release captain for Q1 2026."
   }
 ]
}

